{"archetypes":[{"name":"stub-gate-mechanics","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan's G1/G2/G3 fixtures depend on GH_VIEW_SECOND_HEAD_OID enabling the fake-gh counter and GH_VIEW_FLIP_AT_CALL firing at the exact claimed call number; a mismatch in the counter-gate logic silently produces wrong MERGE_STATE values or wrong call counts.","prompt_body":"Read the fake-gh `view` handler in `scripts/test-merge-pr.sh` (approx. lines 48–72) and trace each planned G sub-case fixture through the counter-gate logic: the `GH_VIEW_SECOND_HEAD_OID` non-empty guard, the `_count` increment, the `GH_VIEW_SECOND_MERGE_STATE` fallback, and the `GH_VIEW_FLIP_AT_CALL` comparison. Verify that G1 (persistent `__EMPTY__`) and G2 (persistent `UNKNOWN`) produce the right stub response on every one of the five expected stub calls, and confirm the `__EMPTY__` sentinel path (which prints `null` for `mergeStateStatus`) is exercised on calls 2+ when `GH_VIEW_SECOND_MERGE_STATE=__EMPTY__` is set. Verify G3's flip fires exactly at call 3 and not earlier, producing `MERGE_STATE=CLEAN` so the helper breaks after two retry attempts. Also determine whether `GH_VIEW_SECOND_HEAD_OID` is actually required to make the `assert_command_count` assertions work, or whether `gh.log` records all invocations unconditionally regardless of counter-gate state. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"sibling-doc-sync","focus_area":"risk-integration","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan explicitly omits scripts/merge-pr.md from the file list, but that file contains prose (\"short-circuits with error\", \"routes through the existing empty/UNKNOWN short-circuit paths\") that directly and inaccurately describes the initial-UNKNOWN behavior being changed; the script-md-siblings rule requires updating sibling docs in the same PR as any behavior change.","prompt_body":"Read `scripts/merge-pr.md` in full, focusing on the `error` row in the MERGE_RESULT enum table (line 24), the Safety Invariant condition 2 (around line 39), and the Batched Discovery paragraph (around line 64). Identify which prose phrases will become inaccurate after the initial-UNKNOWN 4-retry loop is added — specifically any use of \"short-circuits\" or \"short-circuit paths\" that implies immediate failure rather than retry-then-fail. Check whether the existing post-force-push 3-retry description (around line 58) creates a structural precedent that obligates a symmetric description of the new initial-check 4-retry path. Cross-check the plan's stated justification for omitting this file (\"the enum itself is unchanged\") against the `script-md-siblings` rule's edit-in-sync requirement and the Batched Discovery paragraph's explicit \"Failure handling is unchanged\" claim, which will be concretely false after the fix. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."},{"name":"call-count-arithmetic","focus_area":"correctness","weight":1,"rationale":"The plan pins exact gh pr view call counts (5 for Q/R, 3 for G3, 5 for G1/G2) that depend on the helper's sleep-first ordering and max_retries semantics; an off-by-one in max_retries or a misread of the helper's loop body causes pinned assertions in Q2, R3, and the new G cases to fail at CI time.","prompt_body":"Trace the full `gh pr view` invocation sequence for each pinned scenario: G1/G2 (initial UNKNOWN triggers helper with max_retries=4; verify this produces exactly 1+4=5 total calls), G3 (UNKNOWN resolves on the helper's second attempt; verify 1+2=3 total calls given flip fires at counter value 3), Q (CLEAN initial → flush-push → post-push UNKNOWN → helper with max_retries=3 → flip at call 5; verify 5 total calls), R (same path with no flip; verify 5 total calls). For the post-force-push refactor, compare the existing `for _retry in 1 2 3` loop body (which calls `refresh_pr_info` exactly 3 times) with the proposed helper called with max_retries=3 (which also calls `refresh_pr_info` exactly 3 times, once per `while` iteration); confirm the semantics are identical and the Q2/R3 `assert_command_count 5` pins hold. Pay particular attention to whether the helper's \"sleep first, then refresh_pr_info\" ordering adds or removes a call relative to the existing inline loop structure. Cite specific file paths and line ranges for any issues found, and follow the output-format rules from your outer wrapper exactly."}]}
